# Progressive commits

This repo **wants commits without the user asking again**. Implementing a ticket, a bugfix, or a requested change **is** the request to commit.

Do **not** one-dump at the end. Do **not** wait for “please commit.”

## When to commit

After each slice that typechecks / tests:

- Parser, then wiring, then API prompt, then UI — not all of those in one commit.
- A cluster of ACs or one user-visible fix you can describe in a sentence.

Stay on the existing ticket/`fix/` branch. Never commit this work directly on `master`. Do not mix unrelated tickets or drive-by refactors into the slice.

## How

```text
git add <files for this slice>
git commit -m "T03-03: accept ASR compact headings as FLY_HEADING.

Path A must win so Path C cannot turn heading 270 into TURN_DEGREES."
```

Message: imperative subject, **why** in the body, ticket id when there is one. Do not stage secrets, `.env`, `speech-api/.cache`, or untracked QA screenshots.

If a hook rejects the commit, fix it and make a **new** commit (do not `--no-verify`). Do not push unless asked. Do not `--force` on `master`.
